From 76f5fe1ffc722a91cbbb2a7dc9e8903fcd3fd9fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:16:12 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 061/152] power: supply: max17042: Report cycle_count in full
 cycles

The Cycles register of the MAX17042, MAX17047, MAX17050 and MAX17055
accumulates total charge/discharge in 1 % steps of a full cycle (LSB
1 %, range 0 to 655.35 cycles), but the driver exports the raw value.
The sysfs ABI documents cycle_count as a number of full cycles, so a
battery with 79 cycles currently shows 7936.

Divide by 100. MAX77759 keeps the raw value: its scaling has not been
checked here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index d6d7f4278..9f8413e89 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -297,6 +297,10 @@ static int max17042_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
 
+		/* MAX17042/7/50/55: the Cycles register counts in 1 % steps */
+		if (chip->chip_type != MAXIM_DEVICE_TYPE_MAX77759)
+			data /= 100;
+
 		val->intval = data;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_MAX:
-- 
